I had a game yesterday, which was a wonderful illustration to the recent
'to quit or not to quit' discussion. I'm playing an Elf. In my second move 
I hit a trap door. I fall into a small shop. The shop door turns out to be
locked... Now I examine my options:

Nothing that could open the door in my inventory, or in the shop.
If I bash the door the shopkeeper will easily kill me. I have no money
to pay the door, even if I sell all mu stuff.
There is a ring in the shop. I test it - but it is neither teleport nor
polymorph (later turned out to be regeneration).
Apart from the ring the shop has a scroll, 3 potions and some food and 
non-magical armor.
Now, I could test the scroll - but if I do it and it is not teleport, the
shopkeeper will block the door and I'll lose any chance.
One of the potions could be paralysis - but to throw it at the shopkeeper
I'll have to align myself with him, and this is possible only when
he's blocking the door...
I gave up (the scroll turned out to be enchant armor, one of the potions
was paralysis).

Do you still think that one should never quit? (sure, theoretically I could 
wait till some monster appears in the shop, carrying a key or a wand of 
teleport or whatever useful item - only what is the probability?) 

